  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#39029\", \"PowerToys#27001\", \"PowerToys#26396\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys has no tool for managing the File Explorer right-click menu. That means you can't reorder entries, move items out of 'Show more options', or remove leftover entries from old apps. The earlier tickets were closed as duplicates of a single tracking issue, microsoft/PowerToys#33, and another ticket (#35994) was closed as a duplicate of #37919. Please follow and upvote those issues instead of opening a new one. In the meantime, the earlier tickets suggest two options. You can edit the registry by hand, or you can use a third-party context-menu manager to remove stale entries. Nilesoft Shell is one example mentioned in the archive.\"}",
